oesn't snag on  itself and so that prevents future  damage so the exact products i've been  using with amer dimethicone have changed  i've been using the tony and guide  volume addiction conditioner  i was using this last time as well the  problem with this  is that there are a bunch of different  versions and not all of them have amor  dimethicone really high up on the  ingredients list so  usually i look at that as an indication  that there's a bit more in it  i get this from the supermarket and it  goes on half price all the time so every  time i go grocery shopping i  wander through the shampoo aisle and  check and stock up if it's  at eight dollars i've also been trying  this garnier treatment  it is the sleek and shine leave-in  conditioning cream  i got this from iherb i don't know if  it's actually available in australia  it's a leave-in treatment so if my  hair's been feeling a bit rough  after i wash it i'll add a bit of this  on the ends sometimes i'll mix it with  oliplex 3 or 6 to  get that extra bond repair as well so  because ammo dimethicone has been  working so well for me i've been able to  wash my hair more frequently so i wash  it every second day which is my  preferred amount  i have a pretty oily scalp so i've been  using a lot less dry shampoo  i haven't had a lot of success with dry  shampoo because a lot of them tend to  irritate my scalp  so it's really nice that i get to avoid  that now but it does mean that i do have  to re-dye my hair a bit more often  by re-dyeing what i mean is i use  shampoos and conditioners that deposit  color  and my hair isn't like a really bright  color so it doesn't need that much dye  so my favorite that i was using last  time as well is the flash professional  clean blonde violet turning shampoo  with a lot of the other purple shampoos  i've been trying i found that they tend  to dry out my hair and dry out my scalp  my hair can't handle any more drying so  this is  really good i've also been using a new  brand called kin k yn  unfortunately they are a clean brand and  i think you all know my feelings about  clean brands  but they do have a rose gold shampoo and  i haven't really found  other brands that do pink shampoos let  me know if you know of any  i am trying to go for like a pinkish  purple color  right now it's probably a bit too purple  and silvery gray which is great but  not quite the color i'm aiming for yeah  so i've been  alternating between pink and purple  colors to try to keep it within  the color i want if it's a bit too  purple i use the pink if it's a bit too  pink i use the purple  the main reason why i've been going for  pinkish this time even though i love  this silvery purple color  is that in this blended region um  between where it's black  and where it's bleached it tends to go a  bit brassy  and it's a lot easier to hide that  brassiness if you have a warm hair color  so a lot of the time when my hair is  this  cool purple it'll start off the first  day after i wash it looking really good  and then after a while it  just starts looking a bit like brown and  because the brown doesn't really work  with cool it mostly just looks dirty  so this time really i'm going for that  purplish pink color and i'm not really  trying to get it all the one color  so last time i tried to always just have  my hair all one color but this time i'm  kind of okay with it being  slightly different colors everywhere i  think it's partly just because i'm  indecisive about whether i want pink or  purple  the ends of my hair are a little bit  stained from my old die  and so it's a bit brassier it's a bit  hard to see on this camera i think  but it's a bit brassier than the rest of  my hair so i think this sort of mixed  color is working quite well for me and  it's also a lot lower maintenance  so again i do all of my hair coloring in  the shower  nothing stays on my hair for more than  like three minutes because i'm pretty  impatient  last time i used to always dye my hair  once every two or three weeks  and that's just too much effort for me  now so everything is just  colored shampoos and conditioners with  colored conditioner i mix it myself  i put my dye in a lush tub and blend it  out with uberless hydrating conditioner  i got this ages ago and i don't know why  i don't really use it on my hair as  conditioner i just always end up mixing  it  probably because it doesn't have much  ammo dimethicone the die i've been using  is the brand especially plus this is  really good because it's like a three  minute  hair dye unfortunately i can't find this  on ebay  anymore or anywhere really so if you  have another good suggestion for  a three minute hair dye i am really  really keen on that  in the shower i always use a crocodile  clip these just hold  a massive amount of hair this one is  from a brand called cricket i picked it  up  at a hair convention in the before times  it has  these ribbed or dotty grips  which means that it's really easy to  hold on to in the shower  so this can hold like all of my hair  and i have quite a lot of hair  yeah so it holds it all it holds a lot  of it even like when it's doubled up  on top of my hair um yeah so it has this  cool mechanism  where you can hold large amounts  and it'll still grip really hard another  amazing product that i've recently found  is the igk mixed feelings leave-in  blonde toning drops  this is a really intense purple product  that has the same purple dye  as purple shampoos you can mix this into  anything i mix it a lot into  my garnier leave-in conditioning mix i  mix it into my die  if you do get this just to let you know  you press the bottom  of the tube to get the drops out you  don't just like shake it like this and  hope that something comes out  so don't do what i did for 15 minutes  sometimes if i do see a bit of  brassiness here i'll just  put a couple of drops on my hands rub  them together to spread it and then just  do this very quickly and then wash my  hands 